# The Myth of the Two Villages

Long ago, two villages stood on opposite sides of a great river. The Upstream Village had abundant grain, while the Downstream Village possessed skilled craftsmen but poor soil.

One harsh winter, the Upstream elder decided to trust the strangers below. She sent half their grain supply downriver on rafts, knowing the current would triple its value by gathering fish and nutrients along the way.

The Downstream villagers received this unexpected bounty with wonder. Their elder faced a choice: keep everything for their struggling people, or honor the trust shown by returning a generous portion.

